tip: | Look at the plane. | A tube along one grid axis and a long thin slab along the other. Turn anything to the grid first, and the rest is boxes.
tip: 1 | The cross. | Body and wing make a plus laid on the ground. The tail is a small copy of it.
tip: 3 | Wings are thin slabs. | A wing is a top face and a thin edge, two pixels deep. The top catches all the light. Draw the far wing first and the near one last, with the body between.
tip: 4 | One stripe, end to end. | A red line along the body and red wing tips tell the eye that the far parts belong to the same plane.
